\begin{align*}
\mathbf{B} \mathbf{A} &= \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 3 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \\
&=  \begin{pmatrix} a+3b & 2a+4b \\ c+3d & 2c+4d \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
Since $\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B} = \mathbf{B} \mathbf{A},$ we have the following system of equations:
\begin{align*}
a+2c &= a+3b \\
b+2d &= 2a+4b \\
3a+4c &= c+3d \\
3b+4d &= 2c+4d.
\end{align*}
